From 3aec1f223432a61f8aa7225e2caad0c385440e4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:58:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(machine): Tormach 770M+ and 1100M+ - the M with the MX's
 axis speeds

The M+ is an upgrade kit with no manual of its own; per Tormach (via the
contributor, 2026-11-09) everything is the M's except the axis speeds,
which are the MX's. Both ship as built-in Tormach mills for the PathPilot
post: 770M+ = 770M travels/spindle/belts/1.1 kW, 300/300/250 IPM; 1100M+
= 1100M travels/70-7500 rpm/1.5 kW, 300/300/230 IPM; neither rigid-taps.

Pinned by tormach_machines::an_m_plus_is_its_m_with_the_mx_axis_speeds
(compares the shipped files), every_tormach_machine_states_its_manuals_
figures (+2 rows), a_rigid_tap_is_refused_on_a_machine_that_cannot_
rigid_tap (+2) and machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_
declaration.

Fixes #618

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
